<h1>Ed Bannon</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 1a, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent. Endorsed by the Chicago Teachers Union.</p>
<p><a href="https://edbannon.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (edbannon.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Bannon says he puts students first, asking whether each policy decision is best for Chicago&#39;s kids, and campaigns on budget accountability and transparency in school funding. He calls for qualified teachers, counselors, and classroom resources for Northwest Side schools. At a 2026 town hall he said finding ways to increase funding for public education without raising property taxes is a top goal.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Career experience includes serving as executive director of the Six Corners Association. He served about ten years on the Dever Elementary Local School Council and was appointed to the board&#39;s District 1A seat in January 2025.</p>
